{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ d.name }} — the FAIR Digital Object{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h1>{{ d.name }}</h1>
<p class="lead">{{ d.fields.description }}</p>

<section class="card">
  <h2>What this object is</h2>
  <dl class="meta">
    <dt>PID</dt><dd><a href="{{ d.pid }}">{{ d.pid }}</a></dd>
    <dt>Type</dt><dd>{% for t in d.fields.type %}<code>{{ t|short }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
    <dt>Profile</dt><dd><code>{{ d.fields.profile }}</code> (draft, read with the map <code>cca-dashboard-0.1</code>)</dd>
    <dt>Accepts</dt><dd><code>{{ d.accepts|short }}</code> — the kind of object it can render, not a particular one</dd>
    <dt>Licence</dt><dd>{{ d.fields.licence or "not stated" }}</dd>
    <dt>RO-Crate</dt><dd><a href="{{ d.crate_url }}">ROHub's generated crate</a></dd>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>The composition it declares</h2>
  <table class="panels">
    <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Panel</th><th>Renderer asked for</th><th>Settings</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for p in d.panels %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ p.number }}</td>
        <td><strong>{{ p.label }}</strong><br><code>{{ p.kind }}</code></td>
        <td>{% if p.renderer %}<code>{{ p.renderer|short }}</code>{% else %}<span class="muted">any</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{% for k, v in p.settings.items() %}<code>{{ k }} = {{ v }}</code><br>{% else %}<span class="muted">—</span>{% endfor %}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="muted">Each row is a numbered annotation on the Research Object (<code>cca:panel1</code>, <code>cca:panel1Renderer</code>, …).
  A ROHub annotation is a flat property/value pair, so a panel cannot yet be an entity with its own fields; numbering keeps the order explicit.</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>What it is bound to</h2>
  {% if d.dataset %}
  <p>This dashboard was created by forking the template and adding the dataset as a <strong>resource</strong> of the
     fork, so that it is visible in ROHub and can be replaced there; the same binding is also stated on the root as
     <code>schema:object</code> for readers that only look at the crate.</p>
  <dl class="meta">
    <dt>Dataset FDO</dt><dd><a href="{{ d.dataset.pid }}">{{ d.dataset.pid }}</a></dd>
    <dt>Title</dt><dd>{{ d.dataset.name }}</dd>
    <dt>Licence</dt><dd>{{ d.dataset.licence or "not stated" }}</dd>
    <dt>Resources</dt><dd>
      {% for part in d.dataset.parts %}
        <a href="{{ part.url }}">{{ part.name }}</a> <span class="muted">{{ part.media_type or "" }}</span><br>
      {% endfor %}
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <p class="muted">To show another dataset, replace that resource in ROHub with another Research Object PID: a resource
  marked <code>cca:InputDataset</code> wins, and failing that any resource that is itself a Research Object counts as
  the input, so the swap works from ROHub's interface alone. Changing
  <code>cca:panel1Colormap</code> or <code>cca:primaryColorHex</code> changes how it looks. No code is touched either way.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p>Nothing yet: this is the <strong>template</strong>. It says how to display a
     <code>{{ d.accepts|short }}</code>; a fork with <code>schema:object</code> set becomes a dashboard someone can open.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>How it was read</h2>
  <p>fdo-consume read the crate against the contract <code>dashboard-site-v1</code> and reported
  {% for name, status in d.fields._statuses.items() %}<code>{{ name }}: {{ status }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
  {% if d.fields._diagnostics %}Diagnostics: {{ d.fields._diagnostics|join("; ") }}.{% else %}No diagnostics.{% endif %}</p>
  <p class="muted">Validation is <code>INDETERMINATE</code> by design: the draft profile has no authoritative validator yet, so the
  reader states that the terms are present without claiming conformance.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
